    "stem": "A postoperative patient with sepsis requires urgent source control in the operating room. Which answer best describes the most important anesthetic implication?",
    "choices": [
      "use hypotonic maintenance fluid as the primary resuscitation strategy",
      "start early source control and hemodynamic support while reassessing response to therapy",
      "delay surgery until vasopressors have been discontinued",
      "avoid antibiotics until culture results identify the organism",
      "treat lactate elevation with sodium bicarbonate as definitive therapy"
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "This item tests application of the section on Primary Hemostasis in Hemostasis and Transfusion Medicine. The best answer is the option that integrates the topic into a patient-specific anesthetic plan, anticipates complications, and treats physiologic deterioration early. The distractors are common board-style traps: single-factor decision-making, delayed reassessment, ignoring contraindications, or treating a monitor value without correlating it with the patient.",
